{
  "id": "ALAS2023-2026-3125",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2023 - ALAS2023-2026-3125: Important priority package update for rpm",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-09-28 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-09-28 09:00:00"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2023 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-84233:\n\tA flaw was found in rpm. A local attacker could supply a specially crafted `.gem` filename containing RPM macro syntax. When a user or automated workflow invokes `rpmuncompress -x` on this file, the macro expansion occurs during command construction. This allows the attacker to execute arbitrary commands with the privileges of the invoking account, leading to a compromise of confidentiality, integrity, and availability.\n\nCVE-2026-78367:\n\tA flaw was found in rpmbuild. When rpmbuild processes a crafted tarball in tarball mode, a specially designed tar member name can lead to macro injection. This vulnerability allows a remote attacker to execute arbitrary code on the system by convincing a user to build a malicious tarball.\n",
